Reject a fractional duration that does not start with a number.
For an argument with a period whose first character is neither a digit
nor a period, such as "-1.5" or "x.5", the number before the suffix is
empty. strtod() accepts the empty string, so parse_duration_str() went
on to write a '1' into the byte before the argument, outside its
buffer, and then failed with a message quoting "1-1.5". Treat a number
with no digits as invalid, as is already done for a lone ".".

---
 libbb/duration.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/libbb/duration.c
+++ b/libbb/duration.c
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
 		str[len] = '\0';
 		errno = 0;
 		d = strtod(str, &pp);
-		if (errno || *pp)
+		if (errno || *pp || pp == str)
 			bb_show_usage();
 		str += len;
 		*str-- = sv;
